{number: 139}
{title: More Love to Thee, O Christ}
{key: Ab}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[Ab] More love to Thee, O Christ,
[Db] More love to [Ab] Thee!
Hear Thou the prayer I make
On [Eb7] bended [Ab] knee;
This is my earnest plea:
[Db] More love, O [Ab] Christ, to Thee,
[Db] More love to [Ab] Thee,
[Eb7] More love to [Ab] Thee!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[Ab] Once earthly joy I craved,
[Db] Sought peace and [Ab] rest;
Now Thee alone I seek,
Give [Eb7] what is [Ab] best;
This all my prayer shall be:
[Db] More love, O [Ab] Christ, to Thee,
[Db] More love to [Ab] Thee,
[Eb7] More love to [Ab] Thee!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[Ab] Let sorrow do its work,
[Db] Send grief and [Ab] pain;
Sweet are Thy messengers,
Sweet [Eb7] their re-[Ab] frain,
When they can sing with me:
[Db] More love, O [Ab] Christ, to Thee,
[Db] More love to [Ab] Thee,
[Eb7] More love to [Ab] Thee!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
Then [Ab] shall my latest breath
[Db] Whisper Thy [Ab] praise;
This be the parting cry
My [Eb7] heart shall [Ab] raise;
This still its prayer shall be:
[Db] More love, O [Ab] Christ, to Thee,
[Db] More love to [Ab] Thee,
[Eb7] More love to [Ab] Thee!
{end_of_verse}
